<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Support | SmartRecover</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/navbar.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/footer.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/info-pages.css">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Poppins:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.2/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('../includes/navbar') %>

  <main class="info-page">
    <div class="info-container">

      <header class="info-hero">
        <span class="info-kicker"><i class="fa-solid fa-life-ring"></i> SUPPORT CENTER</span>
        <h1>How can we help?</h1>
        <p class="info-lead">
          SmartRecover is the JDCOEM campus Lost &amp; Found platform — it helps students
          report lost belongings, report found items, submit ownership claims, and follow
          the recovery of their items. This page collects guidance for the most common
          situations.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Quick links -->
      <nav class="info-quick-grid" aria-label="Support quick links">
        <a href="/faq" class="info-quick-card">
          <span class="info-quick-icon"><i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question"></i></span>
          <span class="info-quick-copy">
            <strong>FAQ</strong>
            <span>Quick answers about reports, claims, and accounts.</span>
          </span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right info-quick-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        <a href="/privacy-policy" class="info-quick-card">
          <span class="info-quick-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-shield"></i></span>
          <span class="info-quick-copy">
            <strong>Privacy Policy</strong>
            <span>What information SmartRecover collects and why.</span>
          </span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right info-quick-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        <a href="/terms-of-use" class="info-quick-card">
          <span class="info-quick-icon"><i class="fa-regular fa-file-lines"></i></span>
          <span class="info-quick-copy">
            <strong>Terms of Use</strong>
            <span>The rules for using the platform fairly and honestly.</span>
          </span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right info-quick-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
        <a href="/report-issue" class="info-quick-card info-quick-card-accent">
          <span class="info-quick-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-bug"></i></span>
          <span class="info-quick-copy">
            <strong>Report an Issue</strong>
            <span>Something broken or wrong? Send us the details.</span>
          </span>
          <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right info-quick-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
      </nav>

      <!-- Guidance -->
      <section class="info-card info-section" id="guidance" aria-labelledby="guidance-heading">
        <span class="info-kicker">GUIDANCE</span>
        <h2 id="guidance-heading">Step-by-step help</h2>

        <div class="info-guidance-grid">
          <article class="info-guidance-item">
            <span class="info-guidance-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation"></i></span>
            <div>
              <h3>Report a lost item</h3>
              <p>
                Open <a href="/report">Report an Item</a>, choose the <strong>Lost</strong> type,
                and describe the item, where and when you lost it, and add up to five photos.
                Your report appears on the <a href="/items">Browse Items</a> page so other
                students can recognise it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="info-guidance-item">
            <span class="info-guidance-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i></span>
            <div>
              <h3>Report a found item</h3>
              <p>
                If you found something, report it through the same
                <a href="/report">Report an Item</a> form using the <strong>Found</strong> type.
                If the item matches an existing Lost report, open that lost item's details and
                choose <em>“I Found This Item”</em> to submit a Found report linked to it —
                the original reporter is then notified by email.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="info-guidance-item">
            <span class="info-guidance-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-hand-holding-heart"></i></span>
            <div>
              <h3>Submit a claim</h3>
              <p>
                Found an item you believe is yours? Open its details from
                <a href="/items?status=found">Found Items</a> and choose
                <em>“Claim This Item”</em>. You will be asked to describe the item and provide
                proof details plus proof photos. Claims are saved with the status
                <strong>Pending review</strong>, and the item's reporter is notified by email.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="info-guidance-item">
            <span class="info-guidance-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-clipboard-list"></i></span>
            <div>
              <h3>Check your reports and claims</h3>
              <p>
                After logging in, open your <a href="/profile">Profile</a> page. The
                <strong>My Activity</strong> section lists everything you have submitted:
                My Reports (lost and found reports), My Claims with their current status, and
                My Found Reports.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Troubleshooting -->
      <section class="info-card info-section" id="troubleshooting" aria-labelledby="troubleshooting-heading">
        <span class="info-kicker">TROUBLESHOOTING</span>
        <h2 id="troubleshooting-heading">Common problems and what to try</h2>

        <div class="info-faq-like">
          <article class="info-trouble-item">
            <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-key"></i> Can't log in</h3>
            <p>
              Check that you are using the email address you registered with and that
              Caps Lock is off. Repeated failed attempts are temporarily blocked for your
              safety — wait a few minutes before trying again. SmartRecover does not
              currently provide a self-service password reset; if you still cannot get in,
              report the problem from the <a href="/report-issue">Report an Issue</a> page
              while logged into a device where you can sign in, or contact the support
              email below.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="info-trouble-item">
            <h3><i class="fa-regular fa-image"></i> An uploaded image is not visible</h3>
            <p>
              Item photos must be JPG, PNG, or WebP, up to 5&nbsp;MB each, with a maximum of
              five photos per report. If a photo still does not appear, check your internet
              connection, disable browser extensions that block images, and reload the page.
              Your private profile and college ID photos are only shown to you while logged in.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="info-trouble-item">
            <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-flag"></i> Report submission failed</h3>
            <p>
              Make sure every required field is filled in (title, description, category,
              location, and report type), and that your photos meet the limits above. If the
              form keeps failing, note the exact message you see and submit it through
              <a href="/report-issue">Report an Issue</a>.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="info-trouble-item">
            <h3><i class="fa-solid fa-hand-holding-heart"></i> Claim submission failed</h3>
            <p>
              A claim needs a description of at least 20 characters, proof details of at
              least 10 characters, and a valid contact number. You cannot claim an item you
              reported yourself, and only one pending claim per item per student is allowed.
              If you already submitted a claim, you can see it under
              <a href="/profile">Profile → My Activity → My Claims</a>.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <section class="info-card info-contact-strip" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
        <div class="info-contact-copy">
          <span class="info-kicker">CONTACT</span>
          <h2 id="contact-heading">Still need help?</h2>
          <p>
            For account problems, broken pages, or anything that does not work as expected,
            the fastest way to reach the SmartRecover team is the issue form. You can also
            email us directly.
          </p>
          <p class="info-contact-email">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-envelope"></i>
            <a href="mailto:support@jdlostfound.edu">support@jdlostfound.edu</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href="/report-issue" class="info-cta">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-bug"></i> Report an Issue
        </a>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('../includes/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
